{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1459": {
      "title": "Sessional Instructors in Mi'kmaq Studies",
      "description": "Sessional Instructors in Mi'kmaq Studies | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Sessional Instructors in Mi'kmaq Studies Req #222 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, September 1, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, November 6, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY All required documents must be uploaded to Additional Documents with correct titles for each required document. Cape Breton University’s Mi’kmaq Studies and Unama’ki College are seeking applicants interested in teaching specific courses in the fall or winter term on campus, online, or in community. We are seeking qualified L’nu sessional instructors who may be available to teach courses that become available over the next two years. We anticipate ongoing teaching needs in areas such as: Mi’kmaw Language classes Mi’kmaw History classes Mi’kmaw Traditional Governance Other areas of Mi’kmaw knowledge and expertise This is an excellent opportunity for individuals who are interested in exploring a future teaching career, while sharing their knowledge and experience with students. If you are thinking of possible future at CBU, this is a great way to see if teaching is for you! The ideal candidates will possess: A graduate degree in a relevant discipline; and/or applicants who do not hold a Master's degree but have significant traditional, cultural, community-based, or professional knowledge will also be considered for courses that align with their area of expertise. Experience teaching in First Nations communities; Relevant qualifications, experience, or demonstrated expertise in the subject area being taught . TEACHING ON CAMPUS: MI’KMAQ STUDIES Situated within the School of Arts and Social Science (SASS), Mi’kmaq Studies advances Mi’kmaw knowledge and scholarship in support of students developing academic critical thinking skills and awareness of Mi’kmaw perspectives and knowledges. Mi’kmaq Studies fosters engaged citizens who can interact respectfully with Mi’kmaw communities, contribute to self-determination, and understand the importance of upholding treaty and rights-based responsibilities. It is available as a major, double major, and concentration in the Bachelor of Arts (BA) and as a major or double major in the Bachelor of Arts Community Studies (BACS). We are seeking instructors who can teach in this area on campus, and sometimes online. Fall and winter courses typically run for 12 weeks. TEACHING OFF-CAMPUS: IN-COMMUNITY PROGRAMMING For more than 30 years, Unama’ki College’s In-Community Degree Programs have been making post-secondary education more accessible to Indigenous students by offering tailored degree programming across Mi’kma’ki. Students have the opportunity to earn a degree from CBU while studying at home, close to their families and supports systems in addition to receiving specialized student support from CBU. We seek instructors who are interested in teaching courses in-community, which are taught in a more condensed timeline (4 to 8 weeks). Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. Applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as teaching opportunities arise. To learn more about these opportunities, prospective applicants are invited to attend one of two online information sessions. Details, including dates and times, will be posted on the Unama’ki College Facebook page . Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResources@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family Sessionals Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow us to share information with third party advertising and analytics partners and use your information for advertising and analytics purposes. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1452": {
      "title": "Research Manager",
      "description": "Research Manager - Project Homeward Bound  | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Research Manager - Project Homeward Bound Req #189 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, August 25, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, September 25, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University (CBU) is accepting applications for a Research Manager to join a transformative, multi-year research initiative titled Homeward Bound: Enhancing Healthcare, Housing, and Social Support for Aging Rural Nova Scotians. Funded by Research Nova Scotia , this 7-year initiative aims to support aging in the right place (AIRP) by improving the integration of healthcare, housing, and social supports in rural communities across Nova Scotia’s Eastern Health Zone. This ambitious project brings together a multidisciplinary team spanning social work, architecture, nursing, medicine, computer science, economics, and policy, in partnership with communities, government, and academic institutions. Find out more here: www.homewardboundns.ca About the Role This position will be responsible for managing financial and other research operations of the Homeward Bound project, working closely with the Project Manager, Research Coordinator, and Research Leads. The successful candidate will play a central leadership role in ensuring compliance with the project protocols and objectives and applying specialized knowledge to budget management, reporting, and forecasting. Depending on qualifications, the candidate may also support creation and compliance of the project’s data management plan and ethics applications/clearances across multiple institutions. This is a full-time, remote and/or hybrid position reporting to the Co-Principal Investigator overseeing Research & Finance (Dr. Kelsey Harvey) and working within a multidisciplinary team. The appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding and project needs. Key Responsibilities Financial Operations and Oversight • Coordinate financial activities related to the grant. • Develop budgets for the research project(s). • Forecast lifespan of budget, identifying possible gaps and opportunities. • Process expense claims. • Monitor health of the budget. • Support developing estimates of time, human, and financial resources needed to support the research plan. • Document deviations from budget and communicate these to funder. • Work closely with finance office to reconcile budgets. • Prepare budget reports for internal and external partners. • Maintain confidentiality. Depending on qualifications, additional responsibilities may include: Data Management & Governance • Assist with the creation and implementation of the project’s data management plan. • Laise with appropriate parties to communicate the data management plan. • Update the data management plan as needed. • Audit for compliance with the data management plan. • Coordinate data sharing agreements across institutions as applicable. • Maintain systems for de-identification, consent tracking, and secure storage. Ethics • Support the preparation and submission of research ethics applications and amendments across multiple institutions, both academic and in healthcare. • Track ethics applications across multiple institutions. • Keep records related to reporting needs to ethics offices. • Maintain confidentiality. Research Operations & Administrative Leadership • Support coordination of interdisciplinary research activities across project teams, facilitating research meetings and check-ins as needed. • Ensure research staff have the operational supports and tools required to carry out research activities effectively. • Support reporting, documentation, and project tracking in collaboration with the Project Manager and Research Leads. Required Qualifications: • Undergraduate degree in a relevant discipline. • Minimum of 2 years’ experience managing a research project budget of over $1 million annually. • Demonstrated ability to manage a large-scale budget. • Demonstrated experience supporting team development, management, or workforce coordination. • Proficiency in Microsoft Office, including SharePoint and Microsoft Teams. • Excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage competing priorities in a large interdisciplinary research team. Preferred Qualifications: • Master’s or PhD in a relevant discipline. • Experience managing multi-million dollar and multi-year interdisciplinary research projects. • Demonstrated commitment to anti-oppressive, community-engaged, and equity-informed practices. • Experience with qualitative and/or quantitative research methods and interdisciplinary research. • Experience and knowledge related to data management or a willingness to learn. • Experience with multi-institutional research ethics applications. • Experience with community-based and/or clinical research. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: • Complete resume / CV. • Cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant. • List of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered . Salary Range: $80,000 – $90,000 annually Applications must be received by 11:00PM on September 25, 2026. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family NON_UNION Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow us to share information with third party advertising and analytics partners and use your information for advertising and analytics purposes. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1448": {
      "title": "Mailroom/Print Shop Clerk",
      "description": "Mailroom/Print Shop Clerk | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Mailroom/Print Shop Clerk Req #220 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, August 20, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, September 4, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Cape Breton University invites all current employees to apply to any employment opportunities that align with your skills and career goal s. Please ensure you upload you most recent resume (Replace Resume), attach a cover letter in the assigned upload spot.  List of references and any other documents required please add to Additional Documents . All documents should be clearly titled prior to upload. Cape Breton University invites applications for a Mailroom / Print Shop Clerk to join our team in this full-time continuing position . As an essential part of the University’s day-to-day operations, the successful candidate will help keep information, materials, and services moving efficiently across campus. This position is responsible for coordinating incoming and outgoing mail, packages, and courier deliveries; supporting University shipping and receiving activities; and providing day-to-day operational support to the University’s Print Shop. Key Responsibilities : Mailroom & Receiving Coordinate incoming and outgoing mail, packages, and courier services. Sort and distribute mail and deliveries across the University. Prepare shipments, estimate postage, and operate postage equipment. Track missing or time-sensitive shipments and liaise with couriers as needed. Manage university mailboxes and keys. Receive, record, and distribute incoming goods and materials. Prepare receiving and month-end billing reports. Print Shop Support Operate photocopiers, printers, computers, and related equipment. Prioritize and complete print jobs efficiently and within deadlines. Provide cost estimates for internal and external clients. Produce and finish a variety of documents, including course materials, exams, forms, and correspondence. Bind, laminate, and prepare documents as required. Report equipment issues and provide Print Shop coverage when needed. Physical Demands: Requires walking, standing, bending, and lifting (boxes, mail bags, etc). Qualifications: Completion of High School Diploma 1 year of related experience is considered an asset Demonstrated proficiency in the use of computerized systems and databases (MS Office and Email) with the ability to learn updated and/or new software quickly required Ability to work quickly and accurately with attention to detail Demonstrated interpersonal and communication skills, including good customer service Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. The union affiliation of this position is with the Canadian Union of Public Employees (CUPE) Local 3131. Salary level is Band A2. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResources@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family CUPE Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow us to share information with third party advertising and analytics partners and use your information for advertising and analytics purposes. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
